editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/state/movement-006/review-editorial-prompt.md:1720:Vastin did not move. His left hand lay on his knee, and once it opened and closed. His eyes were on the window, on the cupola, or past it, on nothing in particular, the way a man looks at the sky when he is listening for something a long way off. His face was quite still. It was the face of a man reading a figure he had been sure of for forty years and finding that he had misread it on the first day, and every day since.
