### Must fix 1 — chapter 38 forty-day trigger: RESOLVED

The zero-context diff replaces the contradictory missed-sitting trigger with the required fourth-sitting trigger:

> “The code doesn't count missed sittings; it counts days from the close of the fourth sitting, the one that put the record, and if he's out of the jurisdiction on the fortieth of them, it enters him.”

The arithmetic is correct. The fourth sitting closed on day 75; day 76 is the first day after its close, so day 115 is the fortieth. The surrounding proof remains intact: the entry is still *Respondent absent from the jurisdiction; entered as fled*; the house's charter takes a line; three associates' files take a note, making four files with Cael's; and the post-ruling, pre-effect entry remains *Resigned in good standing*. Lira's conclusion also survives: “So we don't run… We walk.”

