editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:114:- Five cross the Line. The book ends on the second day past it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:157:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names. The interval log is day 0. Day 1 is First-day (dawn run and convocation; the instrument is dated this day). Day 2: the Silver floor and the reading room. Day 3: the counter and the north wall. Day 4: the docket at supper. Day 5, Fifth-day: wing three. Day 6, Sixth-day night: the honest floor. Day 7, Seventh-day: rest and Bracken's window. **Day 8, First-day: served**; the procedure runs that night into the small hours of day 9. **The answer is due at the seat in Ostrand by close of business on the twenty-second day.** Karis says the answer's shape will take four days. Brom's sitting is the last Fifth-day of the academic year.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:160:- **Cael:** a bruised right rib, low (the Shield, day 5; "yellow by Seventh-day, gone by the next Fifth-day"). The hip bill from the honest floor was paid on day 7 morning. The right shoulder counted five pushes (day 6). The left forearm's hum is gone. **The Storm stability flag cleared at dawn on day 1** (no notice). Shadow: rent from waking, never used; drifts on day 1 and day 6 (the second that week), both held.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:182:- Hesk's book: the interval log, the dawn entry ("Nothing pulls… Settled… So now it can be priced"), the honest floor's costs (Lira's capitals), the Seventh-day line, "They filed…", and **the first pole**.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:462:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names. Day 9 Second-day: drafting begins (four days to bones). Day 12 Fifth-day: bones. Day 13 night: the integrity section. Day 16: the counter. Two nights of Bracken's reading; the first rain; the weighing. **Day 19, Fifth-day: the answer goes down, three days inside the time** (due day 22). **Day 23: the seat's notice. Day 25, Fourth-day: Jent's conference; Withrow's office that evening.** Day 26 Fifth-day: board line; wing three. Day 27: the coats placed; the honest floor. **Day 30, Second-day: Lira's trial.** Day 31: the district docket's confirmation and the Velmere letter; opened the third evening (day 33). Day 35: Karis's budget; the frames days 35–38. Day 39: the annex convening. **Day 40, Fifth-day (the year's sixth): the first sitting.** **Day 42, Seventh-day: the month's close.** Lira's first meet off the hill is about four weeks away (Rooke's board). Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:577:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names; feet and yards. Day 41 Sixth-day: Vastin's courtesy copy; his petition by that noon's dispatch. Day 43 First-day: the northern junior's file. **Day 44 Second-day**: the seat refuses the petition in the morning; the assistant's market errand; the counsel brings the refusal up at dusk (the house knows a day before Vastin). **Day 45 Third-day**: Vastin receives the denial (the fourth morning) and writes the finding that night; Bracken's baskets; Gault's notice; the correspondent and Rooke; the visitors' log; the piles; a Velmere letter (sealed, r1); the fee office's query; the column filled. **Day 46 Fourth-day**: wing three under the gallery (moved from the Fifth-day for the sitting); Rooke closes the program floor; Umber's transmission. **Day 47 Fifth-day: second sitting** (the exhibits, fifty-one minutes); the release to the faculties; Daeva's statement walked up at supper. **Day 48**: Daeva's letter in the post-room sort; Lira at the rail. **Day 49 Seventh-day** (last day of the inventory's sixth week): the lodge book; "holding a road"; the four queries and the Ternhall letter at supper; Hesk's letter; pre-restriction inventory named; Withrow's story. **Day 51 Second-day**: the honest floor. **Day 54 Fifth-day: the third sitting, the preliminary** — sustained on validity, sustained to full proceedings. Lira's first road meet is day ~63. Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:668:- **The lodge (flag):** the lodge-man (grey beard, bad knee, kept the gate since before Bracken); the wing may read the arrivals book on the Seventh-day; **the road column**, a line every bell since "the year of the thieves", on the order of the chancellor before last; the carter and the gatepost.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:803:**Calendar.** No season or month names; feet and yards; Halcenvane weekdays. Day 77 Seventh-day: Seln at Bracken's counter; two favours; the drop; rain from the morning. Day 78 First-day: the cards read in the annex. Day 79 Second-day: the reach priced. Day 80 Third-day: the mould-room answer; Havel given the letter. Day 81 Fourth-day: the western answer; the grades; the catechism; the case carried to Cael at dusk; the cipher (five arrivals on day 85); the null report; the bridge chained at the third ring after the fourth bell, the town ferry tied up at noon; Havel's sixth entry that night. **Day 82 Fifth-day: the upper ferry; the cut (mid-morning); the reach and the unbinding; the fifth sitting (documentary) at the hour after noon; home over the bridge at dusk (water under the second ring).** Day 83 Sixth-day: schedule posted a day early (the five moved to day 88); fixity; Storm resettles (40 min; 15 min); the doorway (twelve seconds); Rooke. Day 84 Seventh-day: the idle state found by naming at dawn; Karis's curve; the district seat's answer. **Day 87 Third-day: the eleventh of Sowing — eighteen.** Day 88 Fourth-day: the annex (tomorrow at close). Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day. The *fled* default would enter forty days after day 75.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:888:- **Bracken:** winds the counter clock eleven turns on Seventh-days; measured the order's mark with his rule at the lodge window and wrote *Mark a sixteenth low against house stock.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:915:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names; feet and yards; Halcenvane weekdays. **Day 88 Fourth-day:** Lira's strapping off (morning); the case opened in the reading room after supper (five arrivals a quarter apart, Cael fourth, Seln on the eighth bell); the mechanism told to Seln; the seal's grounds revised. **Day 89 Fifth-day:** the counter; Brom's sling off at noon; Lira's question on the north wall at dusk. **Day 90 Sixth-day:** Rooke's "Not yet." **Day 91 Seventh-day:** the Greyvane leaves (Bracken, noon); the enrollment book lent; the clean door found that night. **Day 92 First-day:** the enrollment book returned before the second bell; the honest floor, perception only, after the tenth bell. **Day 93 Second-day:** the four findings. **Day 94 Third-day:** Vastin proposed; five hands. **Day 95 Fourth-day:** Seln reads the closures. **Day 96 Fifth-day:** the note left at the inn on the wharf. **Day 98 Seventh-day:** the borrowed office, the second bell after noon; Vastin eleven minutes early (the Ostrand station's inspection that morning). **About day 103:** Vastin at his desk (the "fifth morning after", having walked six river stations in four days). The *fled* default would enter on day 115 if Cael left. The midyear recess is ahead; not dated. Brom's panel and the ruling share the year's last Fifth-day.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:994:- RATIFIED CALENDAR (binding for M8–M9). Coordinator choice for the finish: the council and the last bout DAY 202; M9 entry DAY 203; the academic year closes DAY 207; the Registry Line is crossed after day 207.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1002:| 70 | Seventh-day | Last day of the nine-week inventory clock when day 8 is counted as its first day. The day-71 meet therefore does not move that clock. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1007:| 98 | Seventh-day | Vastin in the borrowed Ostrand office; M6 closes / M7 enters. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1008:| 99–112 | First-day through Seventh-day, twice | Midyear recess. |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1023:| 201 or 202 | Fifth-day night or Sixth-day | M8's council and last bout. M8 must choose one of these two dates: a later bout would push the year through day 208 and make day 201 cease to be the last Fifth-day. Day 202 gives the ruling, council, and bout separate beats and is the cleaner inheritance. |
