editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1040:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names; feet, yards and paces; Halcenvane weekdays. **Working assumption (flag 1):** the midyear recess is days 99–112; the term after it opens day 113. Day 98 Seventh-day: back from Ostrand; the last carts. Day 99: the empty hill. Day 101: Hesk's letter. Day 102: the argument. Day 105: the lodge; the silence read. Day 106: Lira "Now." Day 107: the orchard. Day 109: the night road. Day 110: the bout posted. **Day 111 Sixth-day: the return bout, lost.** Day 113: term. **Day 117: sixth sitting.** Day 121: Withrow's letters. Day 124: seventh sitting (Havel's window only). Day 125: Brom's schedule. **Day 128 Second-day: Lira's win.** Day 129: Rooke's slate; the night spar. **Day 138: eighth sitting.** Day 145: ninth (log). Day 151 Fourth-day: the year's last supervised bout. Day 152: tenth sitting (the certification request renewed; log). About day 155: Vastin declines. **Day 166: eleventh sitting — merits concluded; two closing sittings and the ruling set down.** **Day 173 Fifth-day: the envelope squared.** **Day 176 First-day: the year's last month opens.** On Bracken's slate: closing sittings on the month's second and third Fifth-days (days 187 and 194 on this count); **the ruling and Brom's panel on its last Fifth-day (day 201), the panel at the second bell.** The page itself states no day numbers after the seventy-sixth (Gault's leaf) and the hundred and seventeenth (Havel).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1161:- Ratified by the audit: Cael wins the last bout two touches to one (day 202, fourth bell); Ephram's RIGHT shoulder out and set, a month in a sling, he stays at Halcenvane; the Blade notice and the fragment count (nine confirmed; the anomaly uncounted); the four call days in Ostrand; Ilsev's six minutes are a return, not a sitting (Bracken's fourteen holds); the certificate form's column heading "evaluator of record" is the certifying office's — Gault declined nothing; Seln's "twice more" stays at TWO; Brom's panel (day 201, second bell) and the Velmere envelope still sealed.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1168:- **Day 201, Fifth-day:** Brom's panel at the second bell; the ruling at the hour after noon. The ruling finds the enrollment lawful and Halcenvane compliant, grants compelled re-evaluation within five weeks, invokes chapter fourteen upon a null result, and makes revocation effective at the close of the present academic year (`manuscript/chapter-51.md:127–157,161–205`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1169:- **Night of day 201 into day 202:** the council opens after the tenth bell; midnight sounds while Brom fetches Ephram (`manuscript/chapter-52.md:259–269`). The five hands therefore rise on **day 202, Sixth-day** (`manuscript/chapter-52.md:319–343`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1170:- **Day 202, fourth bell:** the last bout. Cael wins two touches to one; Ephram's right shoulder is put out and set (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:97–137`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1171:- **Day 203, Seventh-day:** M9 opens the morning after the bout. Four withdrawal forms are on Bracken's counter (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:326–330`; `packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:13–15`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1172:- **Day 207, Fourth-day:** the academic year closes and the scheduled frame would sit; revocation takes effect at that day's close (`manuscript/chapter-53.md:21–35`). The four enrolled travelers must resign before then. The Registry Line is crossed only after day 207 (`STATE_LEDGER.md:994,1022–1025`; `packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:38`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1176:- **Cael:** left forearm bound, five Blade lines wrist to elbow, nothing broken, expected plum-dark for a fortnight; right hip has paid ten bursts, four past the oak's six; right shoulder has paid six pushes at load, one past Norhold's five; two ten-count lanes; headache/slow bill behind the eyes; one spark. No flag. M9 must carry the bruise and road bill so Book 7 can enter with the bruise about a week from gone and no open injury (`manuscript/chapter-54.md:65–137,204–210,298–306`; B6 `BOOK_MAP.md:97–100`; B7 `BOOK_MAP.md:19`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1200:- **Karis's three numbered research boxes** remain roped on the records-hall deposit shelf. Brom has promised to carry all three; M9 already assigns three trips (`manuscript/chapter-47.md:185–205`; `manuscript/chapter-52.md:159–171`; `packets/MOVEMENT-009.md:24`).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1207:**Calendar.** No season, month or English weekday names; feet and yards; Halcenvane weekdays. Day 187 Fifth-day: first closing sitting (the twelfth). Day 190 First-day: Ephram on the oak. About day 193: the east hall rehearsal. Day 194 Fifth-day: second closing sitting (the thirteenth); the seat reserves; call days ordered. Day 197 First-day: down to Ostrand. Day 198: the wool yard; Karis's supplemental. Day 199 Third-day: the district station. Day 200 Fourth-day: the evaluation seat's return (not a sitting); Havel's transfer request written that night, dated for the morning. **Day 201 Fifth-day: Brom's panel at the second bell; the ruling at the hour after noon (the fourteenth sitting).** The council opens after the tenth bell on day 201 and the bell for midnight goes before Ephram is brought in, so **the hands go up on day 202**. **Day 202 Sixth-day:** Withrow in the small hours; the price written; Lira's window; Rooke chalks before light; **the bout at the fourth bell**; the empty yard at dusk. M9 enters day 203. **The district's notice (by a district officer, "tomorrow, or the day after") will name the Fourth-day, day 207, the year's last day; the revocation takes effect at that day's close.** The page states no day numbers.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1213:- **Bracken** wept on the reading-room landing (day 201 night).
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1236:- **Havel:** six sheets numbered one to six and tied with red tape; a *Request for relief from rotation*, signed, dated day 201.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1237:- **Bracken:** thirty-nine copy-sets of the ruling gone by the first bag of day 202; **four sheets of the registry's withdrawal form squared on his counter with a pen, "for morning."**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1242:- **Nine confirmed.** **Blade-adjacent acquired day 202** in the third exchange of the Crown-yard bout (directed, open-eyed, inside an earnest fight Ephram began, the cost written the night before and initialled by four). Notice verbatim (see Protected). The first *earnest — non-hostile*.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1267:- **The evaluation seat's return (day 200; not a sitting):** read by Ilsev with the presiding chair covered; the designation at schedule two's fourteenth line; both returns entire; her note; the contradiction noted; no finding; entered; a fair copy in the porch's public record. No observation from either party.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1268:- **Fourteenth sitting (day 201), for ruling:** the enrollment lawful and the provision standing; the respondent institution compliant, no finding to be entered; **the enrollment basis revoked, the revocation to take effect at the close of the academic year**; **re-evaluation under standard Arbiter protocol at the district seat within five weeks, upon a date to be notified**, the evaluation seat to see to its conduct; the fourteenth chapter upon its result. *Given under the Compact's hand.* Bracken's fourteen came out exactly.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1269:- **Brom's advancement review (day 201):** found for the tier, Iron; unsigned.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1270:- **Pending for M9:** the district's notice of date (the frame-house is reserved for day 207); four withdrawals on the registry's form; a clerk's stamp in the charter folder's right-hand column in the week after the close. File designations unchanged at M8's end. **No resignation is filed in M8. No third move by the faction.**
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1281:- (c) **The four days are "call days"** (my mechanism): an old rule that parties keep within an hour of the seat for four days before a ruling. The evaluation seat uses it; **Ilsev's six minutes are a return, not a sitting** (day 200), with the presiding chair covered and eleven people in the room.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/STATE_LEDGER.md:1299:- **The count of the room (day 187):** 187 on the benches, 19 by office, 206 with Cael. Jent has a clerk (thin, young, unnamed).

