+## (2) Continuity
+
+**Previous-movement seam and calendar — PASS.** Chapter 54 ends after the day-202, Sixth-day bout with Ephram's right shoulder set, Cael's left forearm bound and the four withdrawal forms waiting “for morning.” Chapter 55 opens the next morning, day 203, Seventh-day, at Bracken's counter. Four enrolled travelers file before the day-207 close; Seln, a staff member, files nothing and leaves his four keys. The First-day rewind in chapter 58 is day 204. Chapter 59 explicitly reaches the academic year's last day, day 207, before the Line is crossed. The wet cart camp is the first camp past the Line; chapter 60's shelf is the second camp past it and, because the wet camp used the cart canvas without a fire, the shelf has their first fire. Chapter 60's log dates itself “The second day past the Line, by ours.” The sequence sums cleanly.
+
+**Bodies — PASS.** Ephram stays at Halcenvane with the right shoulder set and a month in a sling. Cael's left forearm remains bound through the road; the five bars blur into a brown-violet bruise, his hand closes again, and the bruise is a week from gone at the shelf. The headache/inability-to-eat bill from the ten-count work arrives and is paid on the road. Lira's right ankle is sound; Brom and Karis have no new injury. Book 7's “no injury open” entry remains accurate while retaining the fading bruise as a closed bill.
