+**People, standings and departures — PASS.** Five cross: Cael, Lira, Brom, Karis and Seln. Ephram stays. Lira retains Iron Rank One and declines the Silver bracket at its full price; Brom remains the unsigned continental Copper champion; Karis retains Ember, Iron Rank Three while forfeiting research standing, allocations and privileges; Cael resigns in good standing; Seln leaves without filing a form. Gault remains evaluator of record, and Vastin remains the Archmarshal/certifying office rather than being relabelled evaluator.
+
+**Counts, objects and documents — PASS.** All three numbered boxes reach the cart, the road and the shelf. Seln's locked case remains under the canvas; Hesk's satchel contains the current log, the full old volume and the sealed Velmere letter; the current log has about a third of its leaves left. Cart, gelding, purse, printed sheet and Ternhall straightedge remain accounted for. Daeva's reply goes west at the ford; the Hesk and Vell letters are written at the shelf, have no return address and remain held. Karis marks the printed sheet from the middle box; Lira records the route separately in her own book.
+
+**Knowledge, progression and reserved truths — PASS.** Nine fragments are confirmed; the Tide-adjacent anomaly remains uncounted. Anchor is idle and undeployed; Shadow is sealed under the witness-can-carry-it-west logic and has not been deployed since the Line. Six people know the falsification/cache history, but only the five travelers carry the integration mechanism into Book 7. The text does not name the Architect, Quieting or the reserved Path term. The old sigil-stone/station relationship remains an observation without maker, purpose or age disclosure.
